Package: bulkrnaseq
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Analysis of Bulk RNA-seq Provider Outputs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Davide", "Capozzi", email = "capozzi.davide99@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Turns the outputs of an RNA-seq provider (gene counts, abundances,
    normalised counts, differential-expression tables, coverage tracks, QC
    reports) into canonical objects and a fixed set of documented tables and
    figures. Analysis modules declare the data levels they need, so a project
    with only a differential-expression table and a project with raw counts
    use the same workflow. Statistical guardrails are enforced in code: no
    sample-level p-value without residual degrees of freedom, seeded random
    steps, and an explicit inference scope for every p-value.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: python3 (standard library only; decodes MultiQC reports)
